From: Qualcommax NSS Builder
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: tune ath11k RX rings for 512M NSS profile

Add a late NSS ath11k backports patch, after the existing memory-profile
and RX-buffer-length patches. Limit changes to the 512M profile.
---
 package/kernel/mac80211/patches/nss/ath11k/999-950-ath11k-shrink-remaining-512m-rx-rings.patch | 29 + 29
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/nss/ath11k/999-950-ath11k-shrink-remaining-512m-rx-rings.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/nss/ath11k/999-950-ath11k-shrink-remaining-512m-rx-rings.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/nss/ath11k/999-950-ath11k-shrink-remaining-512m-rx-rings.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+From: Qualcommax NSS Builder
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: cap remaining RX rings on 512M NSS builds
+
+ath11k's existing 512M NSS memory profile already shrinks TX completion
+and the monitor status/buffer/destination rings. Keep those smaller values.
+Reduce the two remaining 4096-entry RX/monitor rings only when the
+512M memory profile is enabled, without affecting 1G/256M profiles.
+
+Do not alter DP_RXDMA_REFILL_RING_SIZE: it specifies RX buffer bytes
+to firmware, not a ring depth. Keep NSS Wi-Fi offload untouched.
+
+Based on the MX4200 low-memory investigation:
+https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/24154
+---
+ drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h | 4 ++--
+ 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
+
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
+@@ -220,3 +220,3 @@
+ #define DP_REO_STATUS_RING_SIZE		2048
+-#define DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE		4096
++#define DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE		(IS_ENABLED(CPTCFG_ATH11K_MEM_PROFILE_512M) ? 2048 : 4096)
+ #define DP_RXDMA_REFILL_RING_SIZE	ATH11K_DP_RXDMA_REFILL_RING_SIZE
+@@ -228,3 +228,3 @@
+ #define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DST_RING_SIZE	ATH11K_DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_BUF_RING_SIZE
+-#define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DESC_RING_SIZE	4096
++#define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DESC_RING_SIZE	(IS_ENABLED(CPTCFG_ATH11K_MEM_PROFILE_512M) ? 2048 : 4096)
+ 
